# GitHub Repos — Private by Default

Always pass `--private` when creating a GitHub repository:

```bash
# ✅ GOOD
gh repo create responsum-team/my-repo --private

# ❌ BAD — omitting the flag defaults to public on some gh versions
gh repo create responsum-team/my-repo
```

- Never use `--public` unless the user explicitly asks for a public repo.
- If unsure, default to `--private` and mention it in your response.
